-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/OTD> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithology> "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/GD"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI> .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/OTD> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithology> "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/GNR"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI> .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/BADIN> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "A porphyritic, horneblende-diorite and microdiorite, dolerite and olivine-augite hornblendite. Radiometric age: 458 +/- 9 Ma (K-AR whole rock) (Rundle, 1979)"@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/CFCO> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Layered cumulate gabbros and quartz-gabbros, forming the Mosedale Intrusions which have a calc-alkaline/transitional to tholeiitic composition, microgabbro, microgranite with apatite-bearing iron-rich microdiorite, micromonzodiorite and microgranite zones forming the tholeiitic Carrock Intrusions, quartz-phyric rhyolite of the Harestones Rhyolite, and a microgranite named the Iron Crag Microgranite. Several component intrusions have Ordocician radiometric ages (Mosedale Gabbros, Carrock intrusions)."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/CFCOC> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "A microgabbro, cutting the main mass of micrographic microgranite, a narrow marginal zone of apatite-bearing, iron-rich gabbro, microdiorite, micromonzodiorite and microgranite. Radiometric age: microgranite 452.4 +/- 4.1 Ma (U-Pb, zircon) (Millward, D and Evans, J A, 2003.)"@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/CUSH> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Granodiorite."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/DASH> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "[Obsolete]"@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/ESK> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "A pink, medium-grained muscovite granite, aphyric and porphyritic microgranite, coarse-grained granite, medium-grained granodiorite, microgranodiorite, biotite-rich granodiorite, and quartz-mica greisen locally containing topaz and quartz-andalusite rock associated with granite. The age of the granite is 450 +/- 3 Ma (U-Pb, zircon) (Hughes et al, 1996)"@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/GALGR> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Granitic-rock and trace diorite and granite."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/NEDP> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "A potassium feldspar-phyric granite, biotite granite and muscovite-quartz rock, interpreted as greisen."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/OTD> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Granite, granitic-rock and granodiorite with subsidiary gabbro."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/THKD> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "A garnet-bearing, alkali feldspar-quartz-plagioclase-phyric microgranite. Age: 451.0 +/- 1.1 (2-sigma) Ma (U-Pb, zircon), Millward, D and Evans, J A, 2003."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/NEDP> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLowerBoundaryDefinition> "Includes all granite plutonic intrusions of Early Devonian age in Northern England, including the exposed Shap Pluton (SHAP), the Skiddaw Pluton (SKID) and the concealed Weardale and Crummock Water intrusions. The Shap Pluton is the type pluton for this Suite."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/NEDP> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasOldestAge> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/D> .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/DASH> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasOldestAgeValue> "0"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double> .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/NEDP> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasPredominantAge> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/D> .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/CFCOC> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasRockUnitRank> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/RockUnitRank/LD> .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/CFCOH> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasRockUnitRank> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/RockUnitRank/LD> .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/CFCOI> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasRockUnitRank> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/RockUnitRank/LD> .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/CFCOM> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasRockUnitRank> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/RockUnitRank/LD> .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/CRTO> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasRockUnitRank> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/RockUnitRank/I> .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/ESK> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasRockUnitRank> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/RockUnitRank/LD> .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/ENIN> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasThicknessDescription> "A laccolith, about 1km thick, and with an area of about 53 sq. km intruded into the Skiddaw Group and the lower part of the Borrowdale Volcanic Group."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/HAWS> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasThicknessDescription> "At least eight plugs and dyke-like masses within a total area of 19km2, and having a combined outcrop of about 2.6km2."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/MMI> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasThicknessDescription> "The individual sills range from c. 1m (lamprophyre), to about 60m (diorite). An aggregate thickness of 100 - 150m is probable"@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/MSRL> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasThicknessDescription> "Vertical thickness unknown; the surface outcrops extend over 2.5km, with probable extensions at depth on all sides."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/NEDP> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasThicknessDescription> "Not defined."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/SLED> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasThicknessDescription> "Vertical thickness unknown; boreholes show the complex is approximately 16km in diameter."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/THKD> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasThicknessDescription> "A laccolith 0.5 to 1km thick and with an area of about 12 sq. km intruded into the Skiddaw Group and lowermost part of the Borrowdale Volcanic Group."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/NEDP> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasYoungestAge> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/D> .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/DASH> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasYoungestAgeValue> "0"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double> .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/NEDP> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasYoungestAgeValue> "359.3"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double> .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/DASH> <http://purl.org/linked-data/registry#status> <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/reg-statuses/deprecated> .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/BERG> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Bedrock. Occurs onshore. Formed during the Ordovician Period (486.9-443.1 Ma BP)."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/CFCOH> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Rhyolite. Bedrock. Occurs onshore. Formed during the Ordovician Period (486.9-443.1 Ma BP)."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/CFCOI> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Microgranite. Bedrock. Occurs onshore. Formed during the Ordovician Period (486.9-443.1 Ma BP)."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/CFCOM> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Gabbro and quartz-gabbro. Bedrock. Occurs onshore. Formed during the Caradoc Series (Ordovician Period) (458.2-449.75 Ma BP)."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/CMGR> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Bedrock. Occurs onshore. Formed during the Ordovician Period (486.9-443.1 Ma BP)."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/CRGD> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Bedrock. Occurs onshore. Formed during the Ordovician Period (486.9-443.1 Ma BP)."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/CRTO> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Igneous intrusive bedrock. Occurs onshore. Emplaced during the Actonian Substage (Ordovician Period) (451.25-450.5 Ma BP)."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/CUSH> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Granodiorite. Bedrock. Occurs onshore. Formed during the Devonian Period (419-359.3 Ma BP)."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/DASH> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Obsolete name. Occurs onshore. Age not entered."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/LHTO> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Bedrock. Occurs onshore. Formed during the Llandovery Epoch (Silurian Period) - to - Late Devonian Epoch (Devonian Period) (443.1-359.3 Ma BP)."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/NEDP> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Granite with subsidiary greisen. Igneous intrusive bedrock. Occurs onshore. Emplaced during the Devonian Period (419-359.3 Ma BP)."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/NEGD> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Bedrock. Occurs onshore. Formed during the Devonian Period (419-359.3 Ma BP)."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/NEGD1> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Bedrock. Occurs onshore. Formed during the Devonian Period (419-359.3 Ma BP)."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/NEGD2> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Bedrock. Occurs onshore. Formed during the Devonian Period (419-359.3 Ma BP)."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/NEGD3> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Bedrock. Occurs onshore. Formed during the Devonian Period (419-359.3 Ma BP)."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/OTD> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Granite, granitic-rock and granodiorite with subsidiary gabbro. Igneous intrusive bedrock. Occurs onshore. Emplaced during the Devonian Period (419-359.3 Ma BP)."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/POGR> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Bedrock. Occurs onshore. Formed during the Ordovician Period (486.9-443.1 Ma BP)."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/PRTN> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Igneous intrusive bedrock. Occurs onshore. Emplaced during the Ordovician Period (486.9-443.1 Ma BP)."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/SGGR> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Bedrock. Occurs onshore. Formed during the Llandovery Epoch (Silurian Period) - to - Early Devonian Epoch (Devonian Period) (443.1-394.3 Ma BP)."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/SLED> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Quartz-diorite and tonalite with subsidiary diorite and microtonalite and trace aplitic microgranite and pegmatite. Bedrock. Occurs onshore. Formed during the Caradoc Series (Ordovician Period) (458.2-449.75 Ma BP)."@en .
